# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_cochange_uninstall_race.py" "CO-CHANGE/UNINSTALL RACE GATE: PASS" "co-change / uninstall live race" "co-change / uninstall LIVE race (small-findings root fix, SECURITY/privacy — proven LIVE with two connections, not by inspection): the background co-change populate/increment runs on an AUTOCOMMIT connection that calls assert_account_live_with_authority() as ONE statement and the co-change WRITE as ANOTHER, so there is a real TOCTOU window BETWEEN them where the account-wide uninstall purge (holding NO advisory lock — the lock-key asymmetry) can commit its TOMBSTONE and the writer then RESURRECTS co_change rows (private file PATHS) into a purged tenant. The iter-4 audit verified the tombstone is SET but did NOT race the writer live. ROOT fix: the liveness check is now ATOMIC WITH THE WRITE inside the writer's own statement-txn — both ingest_cochange_with_authority and co_change_filter_unseen_commits_with_authority row-lock the account FOR SHARE (conflicts with the purge's UPDATE + the erase's DELETE, so they serialize) then refuse (42501) if tombstoned; and the purge/erase now lock the account FOR UPDATE FIRST so a concurrently-committed legit write is reaped, not stranded. Proven: (A) post-tombstone write REFUSED + zero rows; (B) seen-commit ledger guarded too; (C) concurrent serialization leaves no residue either ordering; (D) structural guard present; (E) the live path still lands" "co-change / uninstall live race (the autocommit-gap resurrection is closed by an in-txn FOR-SHARE+tombstone guard in both co-change writers + a FOR-UPDATE serialize-first in purge/erase; raced live across two connections) — privacy/GDPR-critical" 18
